{"files":[{"content":"#include <bits/stdc++.h>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nint A[1000][1000];\n\ntypedef long long ll;\n\nll solve(int m, int n, int k) {\n  const int paired = min(m, n);\n  const int scanned = max(m, n);\n  const size_t stride = static_cast<size_t>(scanned);\n  vector<int> prefix((static_cast<size_t>(paired) + 1) * stride, 0);\n\n  if (m <= n) {\n    for (int i = 0; i < m; ++i)\n      copy_n(A[i], scanned,\n             prefix.data() + (static_cast<size_t>(i) + 1) * stride);\n  } else {\n    for (int i = 0; i < m; ++i)\n      for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j)\n        prefix[(static_cast<size_t>(j) + 1) * stride + i] = A[i][j];\n  }\n\n  // Build boundary-major summed-area prefixes once.\n  for (int boundary = 1; boundary <= paired; ++boundary) {\n    int *current = prefix.data() + static_cast<size_t>(boundary) * stride;\n    const int *previous = current - stride;\n    int row_prefix = 0;\n    for (int pos = 0; pos < scanned; ++pos) {\n      row_prefix += current[pos];\n      current[pos] = previous[pos] + row_prefix;\n    }\n  }\n\n  vector<int> keys(scanned);\n  unordered_map<ll, ll> h;\n  ll ans = 0;\n  for (int first = 0; first < paired; ++first) {\n    const int *upper = prefix.data() + static_cast<size_t>(first) * stride;\n    for (int last = first + 1; last <= paired; ++last) {\n      const int *lower = prefix.data() + static_cast<size_t>(last) * stride;\n      int *sums = keys.data();\n      // Each position independently produces a complete band-prefix key.\n#pragma GCC ivdep\n      for (int pos = 0; pos < scanned; ++pos)\n        sums[pos] = lower[pos] - upper[pos];\n\n      // Frequency queries and insertions retain their original scan order.\n      h.clear();\n      h[0] = 1;\n      for (int pos = 0; pos < scanned; ++pos) {\n        const ll s = sums[pos];\n        ans += h.find(s - k) != h.end() ? h[s - k] : 0;\n        h[s]++;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  return ans;\n}\n\nint main() {\n  int k, m, n;\n  cin >> k >> m >> n;\n  memset(A, 0, sizeof A);\n\n  for (int i = 0; i < m; i++)\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; j++)\n      cin >> A[i][j];\n\n  cout << solve(m, n, k) << endl;\n  return 0;\n}\n","path":"src/main.cpp"}],"hypothesis":"Hoisting prefix recurrences into a one-time summed-area table should shorten each band's dependency chain: contiguous SIMD differences produce complete prefix keys before ordered frequency counting.","notes":"Retains smaller-dimension pairing and signed-input counting. Prefix values fit int under the stated bounds; frequencies and answers remain 64-bit. No commands or measurements performed.","research":{"queries":[],"urls":[]},"sources_kept":[],"transformations":["Build an oriented, boundary-major summed-area table once instead of repeatedly accumulating raw bands.","Generate each band's prefix keys with a dependency-free GCC ivdep subtraction loop, eliminating the per-band scalar prefix recurrence."]}